Test vectors made by the minisign tool itself (0.11, Alpine), so the Go
verifier is held to the real format rather than to its own idea of it.

  vector.pub              public half of a key made for this with `minisign -G -W`
  vector.txt              the signed message
  vector.txt.minisig      `minisign -S` (prehashed, "ED")
  vector-legacy.minisig   `minisign -S -l` (legacy, "Ed")

The secret half was made in a throwaway container and never written anywhere
else. Nothing trusts this key: it is not in any keyring, and no image ships it.
Every other key in these tests is made fresh by the test that uses it.
